From 59aa38a64c0c00a4b965ca3d99b1561b03667009 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 03:48:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0191: Nav shimmer generalized into a notification-driven
 unread system, plus quest chain discovery

Follow-up to patch 0190's Discovered Quests shimmer: generalize the
one-off chain-only rotating border-light into a real extension of the
notification system, covering every tab and every sub-tab (Vendors,
Harvest, Lore, Raids, Statistics, Hatchery), driven by actual unread
notifications rather than a bespoke boolean, clearing on visit.

- NotificationEntry.targetSubTab, GameState.tabAcknowledged
  (id-based, matching notificationsSeenId's own established shape)
  and chainsSeenOnBoard. SAVE_VERSION 42->43, migration 42 backfills
  both defensively.
- GameEngine.acknowledgeTab(tab, subTab?), requestTab generalized to
  carry a sub-tab (replacing the old Hatchery-only mechanism
  entirely), quest chain discovery notification wired into the
  chainBoard regeneration point (correctly deferring to the existing
  first-ever-chain modal).
- attention.ts: TAB_SUBTABS (6 panels, including the previously
  undocumented Hatchery Nests/Pets split), isTabUnread, isNavTabUnread.
- Audited and promoted 6 existing notifications to banner:true (vendor
  level-up with per-vendor targetSubTab, Trade Route unlock, set bonus
  activation, hero/pet recovery, egg found from a quest).
- All 6 sub-tabbed panels wired: deep-link consume, acknowledge-on-
  switch, unread-dot on each sub-tab button. MenuWindow generalized
  to isNavTabUnread for every tab.
- CSS: .chain-available -> .nav-tab-unread (generalized), new
  .subtab-unread pulsing dot for sub-tab buttons.

No changes to quest chain data, board generation, or QuestManager
itself -- purely the notification/acknowledgement plumbing and its UI
wiring.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and npx vite build --config
vite.web.config.ts both pass clean. No remaining references to the
removed chainQuestAvailable boolean or the old Hatchery-only
requestedHatcherySubTab/requestHatcherySubTab/
consumeRequestedHatcherySubTab trio. SAVE_VERSION chain confirmed
contiguous (40->41->42->43).
